  "expected_answer": "Brief saved, state written, brand set; the line stops at keys: EXA_API_KEY (and MODEL_API_KEY / RESEND_API_KEY unless reused from an app that already runs) must be typed by the operator at a hidden prompt: python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret EXA_API_KEY.",
  "final_text": "I made Harbor Desk, but it's stopped at the keys step: it needs service keys that only you can enter.\n\n**Done so far**\n- I saved the brief to `briefs/harbor_desk.md` and created the app, `harbor_desk`. It's built on the standard starting codebase, set to go on Vercel under the project name `harbor-desk`, with web search on and the browser off.\n- Your workspace (Harbor Pilots), owner and two members are set, and the app is branded \"Harbor Desk\" in #0B6E4F.\n- I didn't need to add any custom code, a second workspace, a package or a custom web address.\n\n**Where it stopped**\nThe app needs 6 keys before it can go live: `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`, `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`, `RESEND_API_KEY`, `PLATFORM_NOTIFY_FROM`, `EXA_API_KEY` and `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`.\n\nFirst I tried copying them from `beta_app`, your one finished app. Vercel on this machine won't hand out saved key values, so the copy failed and nothing was written. That means each key has to be entered once by you.\n\n**The one thing I need now: your Cloudflare account ID**\nThe app uses your Cloudflare account to store the shared document room. This takes about 2 minutes:\n\n1. Open a second terminal window on the factory machine. Use a separate window, not this chat, so the value never shows up here.\n2. Go to the factory folder and run:\n   ```\n   python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID\n   ```\n3. It tells you where to find the value, then asks you to paste it. What you paste stays hidden on screen, goes straight to Vercel, and isn't saved in any file here.\n4. Come back and tell me \"done\".\n\nAfter that I'll walk you through the other five the same way, one at a time.\n\n**After the keys**\nThe next step is the first deploy to Vercel. I'll ask for your yes before I start it. Then the five test runs follow, and the signed-in checks will need a six-digit code from someone who can sign in.",
